CORE
main.c

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* equal indices, equal elements: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* different indices may differ: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
An array no assignment defines (a nondet local) keeps its Ackermann
The array is sized above MAX_FLATTENED_ARRAY_SIZE bits, so it goes through
the array theory (arrayst), not flattening.
